Local changes: browser-worker bindings for legacy runtime globals; complete
unmodified Russian dictionary and voice from the same upstream revision added
to the emulated filesystem; Unicode input converted to UTF-8 before synthesis.
The upstream English dictionary, phoneme rules and samples are unmodified.
No dictionary has been truncated and no speech asset is fetched at runtime.
Regenerate with node scripts/prepare-speech.mjs. A verified local upstream
checkout may be supplied as its first argument. Pinned source checksums are
recorded in that script.

The engine uses formant synthesis. Its audible offline fallback does not claim
to sound like a human or a neural voice. Installed browser voices are preferred
when available.
